 (scope . "Repaired v1.00.30 W4 guarded compiled-root activation (issue #9690): .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/restore-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/setup-racket/action.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt, scripts/ci/prepared-env-report.rkt, ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root-workflow.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt, tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt, artifacts/ci-recovery/v1.00.30-w4/** and artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w2/**, reviewed read-only against the frozen W4 wave doc in .planning/campaigns/96974d2cd97b152f99d296d6956f13b4f3b2bc4f79428894f74a1f3df49753d8/plan-snapshot/ and the BLOCKED-w4 repair list.")
 (report . "Round 3 review is solicited against implementation head b02e44644b8750cf7c06216a99d094fee22826f0; this entry is updated with that verdict (and its narrative) before the implementation PR is merged, so the delivered trio carries an APPROVED verdict bound to the reviewed head. History: round 1 (independent review of the first repaired head) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with three blocking findings — the fast-env producer never passed the compiled-root input (so no consumer could ever hit the root), setup-racket's pre-resolution step invoked `compiled-root run` with no --module which the CLI refused, and the branch carried a merge commit instead of a linear content history. All three were fixed and independently reproduced: the blocked head ce13d0388 has zero compiled-root input lines in ci.yml and fails the no-module run (raw/red-first-review-fixes.txt), and the history was flattened to single-parent content commits on fc1a6fa36. Round 2 returned REQUEST_CHANGES with five findings: the retained chain capture still showed a failed metrics lint (superseded by a green re-run on the resynced tree), the trio was still the stale blocked record (rebound here), the worktree branch was still named campaign/v1.00.30-w4-repair (renamed), setup-racket could touch a restored root without an explicit opt-in (the resolution step is now gated on a resolution-mode input and ci.yml passes compiled-root-mode at the fast-shard call site), and the zero-module run behaviour had no committed test coverage (two CLI-level cases were added). The W2 checkpoint pin cascade was re-stamped for the changed setup action. The wave's declared Verify chain is green end to end and retained at raw/verify-chain.txt."))